      "message": "Comment by Claude:\n\n\u003e  Cipher.getInstance() is relatively expensive (SPI lookup + reflection). For high-traffic deployments, creating a new Cipher on every token read/write will be a performance hotspot. GCM ciphers cannot\n  be safely shared or reused across threads without synchronisation (GCM is stateful), but a ThreadLocal\u003cCipher\u003e pool is a common, safe pattern here.",
